{
  "Comment": "UY nightly incremental (UY-043.3): fetch, then silver for the years fetch marked, then the GX gate over all of silver (UY-043.4). Input: {\"dry_run\": true|false}; missing means false. Rendered by pipeline.tf, checked by tests/unit/sorteos/test_uy_pipeline_asl.py and, against AWS, by scripts/uy_sfn_validate.py.",
  "StartAt": "Defaults",
  "TimeoutSeconds": ${execution_timeout_seconds},
  "States": {
    "Defaults": {
      "Comment": "A console start with {} must behave like the schedule's {\"dry_run\": false}, so the input is merged over the defaults. Anything else the input carries is kept and ignored.",
      "Type": "Pass",
      "Parameters": {
        "input.$": "States.JsonMerge(States.StringToJson('{\"dry_run\": false}'), $, false)"
      },
      "OutputPath": "$.input",
      "Next": "CheckInput"
    },
    "CheckInput": {
      "Comment": "The Lambdas read dry_run with bool(), so the string \"false\" would be a dry run and 1 a real one. Only a JSON boolean gets through.",
      "Type": "Choice",
      "Choices": [
        {
          "Variable": "$.dry_run",
          "IsBoolean": true,
          "Next": "Fetch"
        }
      ],
      "Default": "BadInput"
    },
    "BadInput": {
      "Type": "Fail",
      "Error": "BadInput",
      "Cause": "dry_run must be true or false (a JSON boolean). Nothing was fetched."
    },
    "Fetch": {
      "Comment": "Retries only Lambda's own service errors (the function never ran). An error of the function itself is not retried: a second try would ask the site again for up to 400 pages, and the next night catches up anyway (window_start, owner UY-043.3 3a).",
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::lambda:invoke",
      "Parameters": {
        "FunctionName": "${fetch_function_arn}",
        "Payload": {
          "mode": "incremental",
          "dry_run.$": "$.dry_run"
        }
      },
      "ResultSelector": {
        "report.$": "$.Payload"
      },
      "ResultPath": "$.fetch",
      "Retry": [
        {
          "ErrorEquals": [
            "Lambda.ServiceException",
            "Lambda.AWSLambdaException",
            "Lambda.SdkClientException",
            "Lambda.TooManyRequestsException"
          ],
          "IntervalSeconds": 10,
          "MaxAttempts": 3,
          "BackoffRate": 2
        }
      ],
      "Next": "Silver"
    },
    "Silver": {
      "Comment": "Always runs: with no pending year it only rewrites draw_gaps (~2 s), so no Choice is needed. One retry of anything: it is idempotent, and it clears PENDING#silver only if rev did not move (UY-043.2).",
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::lambda:invoke",
      "Parameters": {
        "FunctionName": "${silver_function_arn}",
        "Payload": {
          "pending": true,
          "finalize": true,
          "dry_run.$": "$.dry_run"
        }
      },
      "ResultSelector": {
        "report.$": "$.Payload"
      },
      "ResultPath": "$.silver",
      "Retry": [
        {
          "ErrorEquals": [
            "Lambda.ServiceException",
            "Lambda.AWSLambdaException",
            "Lambda.SdkClientException",
            "Lambda.TooManyRequestsException"
          ],
          "IntervalSeconds": 10,
          "MaxAttempts": 3,
          "BackoffRate": 2
        },
        {
          "ErrorEquals": [
            "States.ALL"
          ],
          "IntervalSeconds": 60,
          "MaxAttempts": 1
        }
      ],
      "Next": "ValidateSilver"
    },
    "ValidateSilver": {
      "Comment": "The GX gate (D30): a Glue 5.0 job that reads all of uy/silver/ and writes nothing, so it also runs in a dry run, over the silver that is there. .sync waits for the job, and a failed expectation fails the job, this state and the execution (owner, UY-043.4 3a): the alarm mails it. No Retry: the same silver gives the same verdict. The verdict itself is in /aws-glue/jobs/output, stream = job_run_id.",
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::glue:startJobRun.sync",
      "Parameters": {
        "JobName": "${dq_job_name}",
        "Arguments": {
          "--RUN_ID.$": "$$.Execution.Name"
        }
      },
      "ResultSelector": {
        "job_run_id.$": "$.Id",
        "state.$": "$.JobRunState",
        "started_on.$": "$.StartedOn",
        "completed_on.$": "$.CompletedOn",
        "billed_seconds.$": "$.ExecutionTime"
      },
      "ResultPath": "$.dq",
      "End": true
    }
  }
}
